{"content":[{"c":["SHIHOR"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Body of water in Egypt. The name is Egyptian and is given as a boundary of the land to be possessed by the Hebrews (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.13.3","r":"Josh.13.3","rawR":"Josh.13.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.13.3","value":"Josh.13.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 13:3"},"). ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.13.5","r":"1Chr.13.5","rawR":"1Chr.13.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.13.5","value":"1Chr.13.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"First Chronicles 13:5"}," refers to Shihor as the southwestern limit of Israelite settlement in the time of David. Isaiah speaks of grain from the region of Shihor as a source of income for the city of Sidon (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.23.3","r":"Isa.23.3","rawR":"Isa.23.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.23.3","value":"Isa.23.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 23:3"},"). Jeremiah describes Shihor as “the waters of the Nile” (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.2.18","r":"Jer.2.18","rawR":"Jer.2.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.2.18","value":"Jer.2.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 2:18"},"). Some believe that the Shihor was the easternmost branch of the Nile Delta. Others identify the Shihor with the Wadi el-Arish, 90 miles (144.8 kilometers) east of the Suez Canal. Still others identify it with the Brook (or River) of Egypt, a body of water whose precise location cannot be determined with certainty."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=BrookofEgypt_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"BrookofEgypt_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"BrookofEgypt_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Brook of Egypt"},"; ",{"href":"?item=NileRiver_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"NileRiver_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"NileRiver_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Nile River"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Shihor","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 13:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.13.3","rawQueryValue":"Josh.13.3","sourceRefExact":"Josh.13.3"},{"anchorText":"First Chronicles 13:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.13.5","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.13.5","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.13.5"},{"anchorText":"Is 23:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.23.3","rawQueryValue":"Isa.23.3","sourceRefExact":"Isa.23.3"},{"anchorText":"Jer 2:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.2.18","rawQueryValue":"Jer.2.18","sourceRefExact":"Jer.2.18"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"26be37e7f4d7db2dc76a1596f2347ed12f2bf03c1305b55f451f6dc9ab37fe24","sourceItemName":"Shihor","sourceItemOrder":314,"sourceMember":"Articles/S.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Shihor","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Shihor","title":"Shihor","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}